{
  "_doc": "Phrase-key bridging fixture. Mirrors the pathology measured on the live store (177 of 204 3+-token keys were singletons): a memory whose ONLY key is a memory-specific phrase, in a store where an atomic hub for the same concept already exists. Each 'bridge' query asks with the ATOMIC concept and expects the orphan memory — reachable pre-bridge only by repeating the phrase verbatim. Contents are deliberately worded away from the query so 1-hop content similarity cannot carry them (same design as assoc-fixture's assoc2). 'direct' queries are controls that must not regress. 'precision' queries name a concept whose atomic key shares a TOKEN with an off-topic phrase key — bridging must NOT drag that memory in. 'notfound' must return nothing. Ground truth = expect[] of memory ids. The d-* memories are distractors: ordinary project facts on atomic keys, none of them any query's answer. They exist so top-10 is selective (60 memories) — at 16 the window covered most of the store and every condition scored 100%.",
